   "note": "Title page leaf 7. RESOLVES the OCR-damage publisher conflict: the page reads 'PUBLISHED BY THOMAS LONGWORTH', so phase 0b's 'THOMAS LOKCWORTH' was damage, not a different house. The regnal formula gives the year independently ('FIFTY-FIRST YEAR OF AMERICAN INDEPENDENCE' = 1775+51 = 1826) and the imprint prints 1826. It states an approximate entry count, 'exceeding twenty-seven thousand', against the 1839 volume's 'near thirty-nine thousand' -- the same series, thirteen years apart, so the two are a growth measurement. It also carries the SAME Othello epigraph as the 1839 volume ('Who steals my purse, steals trash -- But he who borrows my DIRECTORY, filches me Most villanously'), a house signature spanning both."
  },
